ele-messenger (1.4.3-1) resolute; urgency=high

  * Security fixes from a source review, each with a regression test in
    tests/server_test.py:
    - No default admin account with PIN 1234; one still holding the
      default is removed at startup.
    - Group messages sent over the websocket check membership, the same
      shared check as the HTTP path.
    - Machine sessions judge the real caller (X-Real-IP from nginx, trusted
      only from this machine) instead of treating every proxied caller as
      local.
    - Closing an older websocket no longer takes the user's newer one
      offline.
    - Server settings can be changed only by a program on the server
      itself, and only known settings.
    - Who is online and the connection log are for signed-in callers;
      /online still answers for reachability checks.
    - The fleet sync token is accepted in an X-Fleet-Token header, so it
      stays out of access logs.
  * Web client: secret chats refuse to send instead of sending readable
    text when the page can't encrypt (plain http, no PIN, no peer key).

 -- thefangeddeity <thefangeddeity@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:00:00 +0000

