ele-messenger (1.4.1-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Server: every database connection is closed. A long-running server
    leaked one per request until it could no longer open its database,
    and the web client then showed a login form.
  * ELE Mesh: machines tell each other their names inside the encrypted
    link; messages sent without a name carry the machine's name; elemesh
    lists the ELE servers it finds on the network.
  * The mesh page and the desktop app share the suite's look and layout.

 -- thefangeddeity <thefangeddeity@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 06:10:00 +0000

ele-messenger (1.4.0-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * ELE Mesh: elemesh, a per-machine daemon that carries chat between
    machines over Bluetooth and Wi-Fi with no router, server or internet;
    store-and-hold, relaying, and catch-up after time apart.
  * ele: a desktop client (Linux, macOS, Windows) for the mesh. It uses the
    local elemesh or runs its own node, lists the ELE machines and ELE
    servers around, and opens a server's page.
  * A message keeps its timestamp and identity however it arrived, so the
    same message reaching a node by two paths is stored once.
  * The packaged web client and server match the source tree again.

 -- thefangeddeity <thefangeddeity@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000

ele-messenger (1.3.6-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Server binds 127.0.0.1 instead of 0.0.0.0: the package installs an nginx
    snippet that proxies to localhost and the client talks to nginx, so the
    wider bind only exposed an unauthenticated API on the LAN and tailnet.
  * Node identity removed from the tree (config.json is node-local now,
    config.example.json tracks its shape; the Flutter default host is empty).
  * Compiled client build output dropped from the repo.

